{"id":"dca22faafaee72fb","group":"73","path":"73/73-thm-nfa-determinization.md","title":"DFA–NFA Language Equivalence","display":"thm-dfa-nfa-equivalence — DFA–NFA Language Equivalence","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Introduction to Automata Theory, Languages, and Computation (Hopcroft, Motwani, Ullman; 3rd ed., 2007)","book_abbrev":"73","label":"73-thm-nfa-determinization","aliases":["73-thm-nfa-determinization","73-thm-dfa-nfa-equivalence"],"display":"thm-dfa-nfa-equivalence — DFA–NFA Language Equivalence","depends_on":["[[73-df-nfa-subset-construction]]","[[73-df-dfa-language-semantics]]","[[73-df-nfa-language-semantics]]","[[73-df-finite-words-and-languages]]"],"source_id":"HMU2007","source_ref":"§2.3, print pp. 55–65; PDF pp. 77–87","source_status":"third-edition-topic-mapped; inherited-local-review; not-a-line-by-line-source-proof-certificate","reviewed_on":"2026-10-24","legacy_source_id":"HU1979","legacy_source_ref":"§2.3, Theorem 2.1, pp. 19–24; local explicit subset construction","legacy_source_status":"local-formalization; source-section-located; proof scope recorded in review","revision_round":"pdf-third-edition-20261024","edition_role":"third-edition-core","third_edition_chapter":2},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Introduction to Automata Theory, Languages, and Computation (Hopcroft, Motwani, Ullman; 3rd ed., 2007)"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"73"},{"key":"label","html":"73-thm-nfa-determinization"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>73-thm-nfa-determinization</span><span>73-thm-dfa-nfa-equivalence</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-dfa-nfa-equivalence — DFA–NFA Language Equivalence"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"05d04ddcf190776e\" href=\"?note=05d04ddcf190776e\" title=\"73-df-nfa-subset-construction\">73-df-nfa-subset-construction</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"3b7a967565c86f39\" href=\"?note=3b7a967565c86f39\" title=\"73-df-dfa-language-semantics\">73-df-dfa-language-semantics</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"1d700ea676b35b73\" href=\"?note=1d700ea676b35b73\" title=\"73-df-nfa-language-semantics\">73-df-nfa-language-semantics</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"0a6da8c909717780\" href=\"?note=0a6da8c909717780\" title=\"73-df-finite-words-and-languages\">73-df-finite-words-and-languages</a></span></div>"},{"key":"source_id","html":"HMU2007"},{"key":"source_ref","html":"§2.3, print pp. 55–65; PDF pp. 77–87"},{"key":"source_status","html":"third-edition-topic-mapped; inherited-local-review; not-a-line-by-line-source-proof-certificate"},{"key":"reviewed_on","html":"2026-10-24"},{"key":"legacy_source_id","html":"HU1979"},{"key":"legacy_source_ref","html":"§2.3, Theorem 2.1, pp. 19–24; local explicit subset construction"},{"key":"legacy_source_status","html":"local-formalization; source-section-located; proof scope recorded in review"},{"key":"revision_round","html":"pdf-third-edition-20261024"},{"key":"edition_role","html":"third-edition-core"},{"key":"third_edition_chapter","html":"2"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>固定 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Sigma\">\\(\\Sigma\\)</span> 满足 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Alphabet}(\\Sigma)\">\\(\\operatorname{Alphabet}(\\Sigma)\\)</span>；字母与有限词的类型见 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"0a6da8c909717780\" href=\"?note=0a6da8c909717780\" title=\"73-df-finite-words-and-languages\">73-df-finite-words-and-languages</a>。</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathsf{DFA}_{\\Sigma},\\mathsf{NFA}_{\\Sigma}\">\\(\\mathsf{DFA}_{\\Sigma},\\mathsf{NFA}_{\\Sigma}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L(\\cdot)\">\\(L(\\cdot)\\)</span> (automata and accepted languages, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"3b7a967565c86f39\" href=\"?note=3b7a967565c86f39\" title=\"73-df-dfa-language-semantics\">73-df-dfa-language-semantics</a> and <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"1d700ea676b35b73\" href=\"?note=1d700ea676b35b73\" title=\"73-df-nfa-language-semantics\">73-df-nfa-language-semantics</a>)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>最后两个断言固定 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"N=(Q,\\Sigma,\\delta,q_0,F)\\in\\mathsf{NFA}_{\\Sigma}\">\\(N=(Q,\\Sigma,\\delta,q_0,F)\\in\\mathsf{NFA}_{\\Sigma}\\)</span>，<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Subset}(N)\">\\(\\operatorname{Subset}(N)\\)</span> 见 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-8\" data-note=\"05d04ddcf190776e\" href=\"?note=05d04ddcf190776e\" title=\"73-df-nfa-subset-construction\">73-df-nfa-subset-construction</a>。</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}dfa\\text{-}nfa\\text{-}equivalence}\\vdash\n\\forall L\\subseteq\\Sigma^*\\;\n\\left[\n\\exists N\\in\\mathsf{NFA}_{\\Sigma}\\;(L=L(N))\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\exists M\\in\\mathsf{DFA}_{\\Sigma}\\;(L=L(M))\n\\right]\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}dfa\\text{-}nfa\\text{-}equivalence}\\vdash\n\\forall L\\subseteq\\Sigma^*\\;\n\\left[\n\\exists N\\in\\mathsf{NFA}_{\\Sigma}\\;(L=L(N))\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\exists M\\in\\mathsf{DFA}_{\\Sigma}\\;(L=L(M))\n\\right]\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\forall w\\in\\Sigma^*\\;\\widehat\\delta_{\\operatorname{Subset}(N)}(\\{q_0\\},w)=\\widehat\\delta_N(q_0,w)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\forall w\\in\\Sigma^*\\;\\widehat\\delta_{\\operatorname{Subset}(N)}(\\{q_0\\},w)=\\widehat\\delta_N(q_0,w)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"L(\\operatorname{Subset}(N))=L(N)\\land|\\pi_1(\\operatorname{Subset}(N))|=2^{|Q|}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[L(\\operatorname{Subset}(N))=L(N)\\land|\\pi_1(\\operatorname{Subset}(N))|=2^{|Q|}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>For the nontrivial direction, the subset construction uses state set <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal P(Q)\">\\(\\mathcal P(Q)\\)</span>, initial state <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\{q_0\\}\">\\(\\{q_0\\}\\)</span>, transition <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"S\\mapsto\\bigcup_{q\\in S}\\delta(q,a)\">\\(S\\mapsto\\bigcup_{q\\in S}\\delta(q,a)\\)</span>, and final subsets meeting <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"F\">\\(F\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>Conversely, a DFA is an NFA whose transition values are singletons. Induction on word length proves preservation of acceptance.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"73-df-nfa-subset-construction","status":"resolved","id":"05d04ddcf190776e","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[73-df-nfa-subset-construction]]","embed":false},{"target":"73-df-dfa-language-semantics","status":"resolved","id":"3b7a967565c86f39","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[73-df-dfa-language-semantics]]","embed":false},{"target":"73-df-nfa-language-semantics","status":"resolved","id":"1d700ea676b35b73","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[73-df-nfa-language-semantics]]","embed":false},{"target":"73-df-finite-words-and-languages","status":"resolved"